# TypeScript Standards

## Code Style
- Always use semicolons
- Use double quotes for strings
- Use camelCase for variables and functions
- Use PascalCase for components and types
- Use UPPER_SNAKE_CASE for constants

## Type Definitions
- Define interfaces in [src/types/index.ts](mdc:src/types/index.ts)
- Use strict TypeScript configuration
- Always type function parameters and return values
- Use proper generic types for reusable components

## Component Standards
- Use `'use client'` directive for client components
- Export components as default
- Use proper prop interfaces extending React.HTMLAttributes
- Use React.FC for functional components

## Authentication Types
- User interface includes `uniqueId`, `role`, `permissions`
- AuthContext provides login with uniqueId (not email)
- SUPER ADMIN role has full system access

## Import Organization
1. React imports
2. Next.js imports
3. Third-party libraries
4. Internal components
5. Types and utilities
6. Relative imports

## Error Handling
- Use try-catch blocks for async operations
- Provide meaningful error messages
- Use proper TypeScript error types
- Handle loading states properly

## State Management
- Use Redux Toolkit for global state
- Use React Context for authentication
- Use local state for component-specific data
- Ensure Redux state is serializable (no Date objects, use ISO strings)